mentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Zach Nunn (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Zach Nunn is defending Iowa's 3rd District against Democrat Sarah Trone Garriott in one of the nation's most competitive House races. The district leans slightly Republican, but the national political climate strongly favors Democrats this cycle, and that environment is the central force in the contest. Nunn's incumbency and bipartisan branding offer some protection, while Trone Garriott has out-raised him and holds a cash advantage heading into the final stretch.\n\nIndependent raters uniformly rate this a Democratic flip opportunity, ranging from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets put Democratic odds in the low-to-mid 80s. Public polling is sparse and dated, with the only recent surveys coming from partisan sponsors months ago. Heavy outside spending has targeted both candidates, and the October debate covered Iran, health care and affordability. The forecast calls the race Lean Democratic with meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7301, "margin": 3.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7544, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7522, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7422, "margin": 4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7642, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7587, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7656, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7663, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7741, "margin": 4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7744, "margin": 4.4}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7306, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7274, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7069, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7583, "margin": 4.5